{"cwd": "/sandbox/runs/harbor-dispatch-sonnet5/runs/train-INC-112-r1/harbor-dispatch", "isSidechain": false, "message": {"content": [{"text": "All 27 tests pass. Here's a summary of the fix for INC-112.\n\n**Root cause:** `transitHours` in `src/eta/transit.ts:14` was computing `distanceKm(distanceNm) / speedKn` — dividing a distance converted to kilometres by a speed in knots (nautical miles/hour), mixing units. Since 1 nm = 1.852 km, this inflated every transit time by that factor (~85% too long), matching the reported symptom.\n\n**Fix:** Divide the raw nautical-mile distance by the knots speed directly, since both are already in the same nautical unit system: `distanceNm / speedKn`.\n\nVerified against the incident's acceptance criteria (`transitHours(240, 12) === 20`, `transitHours(90, 18) === 5`), added a regression test for it, and confirmed `distanceKm` (unaffected utility) and the full `npm run check` suite (27/27) still pass.", "type": "text"}], "id": "msg_011CfV9MV7u5qTeUqh4656Za", "model": "claude-sonnet-5", "role": "assistant"}, "sessionId": "e2151d8c-bafe-4580-a277-7784f4afb226", "timestamp": "2026-09-28T03:41:40.424Z", "type": "assistant"}
